Wait, I just realized something. The `FillNetworkDataTlv` function passes `aStableOnly` to `GetNetworkData`. If `aStableOnly` is `false`, then `RemoveTemporaryData` is NOT called. But the check `aDataLength >= mLength` still applies.

Let me look at the callers of `AppendNetworkData`:

```cpp
// mle_router.cpp:2853
SuccessOrExit(error = AppendNetworkData(*message, !aChild.IsFullNetworkData()));
// mle_router.cpp:2943
SuccessOrExit(error = AppendNetworkData(*message, !aChild.IsFullNetworkData()));
// mle_router.cpp:3010
SuccessOrExit(error = AppendNetworkData(*message, !aChild->IsFullNetworkData()));
// mle_router.cpp:3087
SuccessOrExit(error = AppendNetworkData(*message, stableOnly));
```

So `aStableOnly` can be either true or false.

Let me think about this differently. Maybe the vulnerability is not in `FillNetworkDataTlv` but in `AppendTlv`:

```cpp
otError Mle::AppendNetworkData(Message &aMessage, bool aStableOnly)
{
    otError        error = OT_ERROR_NONE;
    NetworkDataTlv tlv;

    VerifyOrExit(!mRetrieveNewNetworkData, error = OT_ERROR_INVALID_STATE);

    tlv.Init();
    FillNetworkDataTlv(tlv, aStableOnly);

    error = aMessage.AppendTlv(tlv);

exit:
    return error;
}
```

`AppendTlv` is:
```cpp
otError Message::AppendTlv(const Tlv &aTlv)
{
    return Append(&aTlv, aTlv.GetSize());
}
```

`GetSize()` returns `sizeof(Tlv) + GetLength()`. If `GetLength()` is set to some value by `FillNetworkDataTlv`, then `GetSize()` returns `2 + length`, and `Append` tries to read `2 + length` bytes from `&tlv`, but `tlv` is only 2 bytes on the stack!

But `FillNetworkDataTlv` sets `length = 0` initially, and `GetNetworkData` only modifies `length` if `mLength == 0` (in which case it stays 0). So `GetLength()` should be 0.

Unless... `GetNetworkData` modifies `aDataLength` even when it fails? Let me check:

```cpp
VerifyOrExit(aDataLength >= mLength, error = OT_ERROR_NO_BUFS);
memcpy(aData, mTlvs, mLength);
aDataLength = mLength;
```

If `aDataLength < mLength`, it exits with `OT_ERROR_NO_BUFS` and `aDataLength` is NOT modified. So `length` stays 0.

